From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Thu, 24 Sep 2026 03:52:46 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 004/148] [ae-patch] Add a Status submenu to the sidebar
 session menu that sets ae.status

omnigent-ae patch P4 (2026-09-24). Right-clicking a session, or opening its
kebab, now shows Status with Working, Blocked, Review, Parked and Reference,
the stored ae.status checked (menuitemradio, aria-checked). The extension SDK
has no menu contribution point, so this is a core patch.

It writes exactly what the Parking Lot page's status buttons write: one
ae.status label through upstream's own PATCH /v1/sessions/{id}, the route the
AE stdio MCP server's omni_set_status uses. The page's Park is label-only (the
note is filed from its Park form), so Parked here is label-only too and its
tooltip says nothing is filed to the task-store; Review is the page's Done.

The labels PATCH does not consult the slot cap, which runs at prompt time, so
Working asks GET /v1/ae/capacity first and refuses at the limit with the
server's count and the working titles; when that route cannot answer, the
count comes from the sidebar's own cache, the same rows the Slots pill counts.
Nothing overrides the cap: "ride unparked" in a prompt stays the only way to
run a fourth. A failed PATCH is a toast carrying the server's detail. A
successful one is painted onto every cached copy of the row in place, as
upstream's pin and archive overlays do.

Logic lives in the new web/src/shell/AeStatusMenu.tsx; the upstream edit is
eight lines in Sidebar.tsx (an import and the owner-gated submenu above the
lifecycle actions). On mobile the items render inline under a Status heading,
since the sidebar's menus have no room for a side flyout there. Tests: the
new AeStatusMenu suite and four cases in Sidebar.aeStatus.test.tsx.

